You are tasked with creating a simple Java program that simulates a library management system. The system should allow users to add, remove, and search for books in the library. Additionally, users should be able to check out and return books.

Your task is to implement the `Library` class, which will manage the library's collection of books. The `Book` class has already been provided for you. You need to implement the following methods in the `Library` class:

1. `addBook(Book book)`: Adds a book to the library.
2. `removeBook(String title)`: Removes a book from the library based on its title.
3. `searchByTitle(String title)`: Searches for a book in the library based on its title and returns the book if found, otherwise returns `null`.
4. `checkOutBook(String title)`: Marks a book as checked out based on its title.
5. `returnBook(String title)`: Marks a checked-out book as returned based on its title.

You should also create a `LibraryApp` class with a `main` method to demonstrate the functionality of the `Library` class. The `main` method should create a library, add some books, perform various operations, and display the results.

The `Book` class has the following structure:
```java
public class Book {
    private String title;
    private String author;

    public Book(String title, String author) {
        this.title = title;
        this.author = author;
    }

    // Getters and setters
}
```

You should assume that the `Book` class has appropriate getters and setters for the `title` and `author` fields.

output:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Library {
    private List<Book> books;

    public Library() {
        this.books = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    public void addBook(Book book) {
        books.add(book);
        System.out.println("Book added: " + book.getTitle());
    }

    public void removeBook(String title) {
        for (Book book : books) {
            if (book.getTitle().equals(title)) {
                books.remove(book);
                System.out.println("Book removed: " + title);
                return;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Book not found: " + title);
    }

    public Book searchByTitle(String title) {
        for (Book book : books) {
            if (book.getTitle().equals(title)) {
                return book;
            }
        }
        return null;
    }

    public void checkOutBook(String title) {
        for (Book book : books) {
            if (book.getTitle().equals(title)) {
                book.setCheckedOut(true);
                System.out.println("Book checked out: " + title);
                return;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Book not found: " + title);
    }

    public void returnBook(String title) {
        for (Book book : books) {
            if (book.getTitle().equals(title)) {
                book.setCheckedOut(false);
                System.out.println("Book returned: " + title);
                return;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Book not found: " + title);
    }
}
```

