            right_height = self.right.height() if self.right else -1
            return 1 + max(left_height, right_height)
```

The `height` method recursively calculates the height of the binary tree rooted at the current node. If the current node is `None`, it returns -1. Otherwise, it calculates the height of the left and right subtrees and returns the maximum height plus 1. This approach ensures that the height of an empty tree is considered as -1.

